<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Power rule: differentiate c x^n (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Differentiate using the <b>power rule</b>. Give an exact answer (no decimals).</p>
[[ if test="notn=1" ]]
<p>Find \( f'(x) \) for \( f(x) = {@expr@} \).</p>
[[/ if ]]
[[ if test="notn=2" ]]
<p>Find \( \dfrac{dy}{dx} \) for \( y = {@expr@} \).</p>
[[/ if ]]
[[ if test="notn=3" ]]
<p>Find \( \dfrac{d}{dx}\!\left( {@expr@} \right) \).</p>
[[/ if ]]
<div>[[ if test="notn=1" ]]\( f'(x) = \)[[/ if ]][[ if test="notn=2" ]]\( \dfrac{dy}{dx} = \)[[/ if ]][[ if test="notn=3" ]]\( \dfrac{d}{dx}\!\left( {@expr@} \right) = \)[[/ if ]] [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[[[ if test="notn=1" ]]<p>The <b>power rule</b>: if \( f(x)=c\,x^{n} \) then \( f'(x)=c\,n\,x^{\,n-1} \). Bring the exponent down as a factor, then reduce the exponent by \( 1 \); the constant multiple stays put.</p>[[/ if ]][[ if test="notn=2" ]]<p>The <b>power rule</b>: if \( y=c\,x^{n} \) then \( \dfrac{dy}{dx}=c\,n\,x^{\,n-1} \). Bring the exponent down as a factor, then reduce the exponent by \( 1 \); the constant multiple stays put.</p>[[/ if ]][[ if test="notn=3" ]]<p>The <b>power rule</b>: \( \dfrac{d}{dx}\!\left(c\,x^{n}\right)=c\,n\,x^{\,n-1} \). Bring the exponent down as a factor, then reduce the exponent by \( 1 \); the constant multiple stays put.</p>[[/ if ]]
<p>Here \( c = {@c@} \) and \( n = {@n@} \), so</p>
\[ [[ if test="notn=1" ]]f'(x)[[/ if ]][[ if test="notn=2" ]]\dfrac{dy}{dx}[[/ if ]][[ if test="notn=3" ]]\dfrac{d}{dx}\!\left( {@expr@} \right)[[/ if ]] = {@ev(step_disp, simp=false)@} = {@ta1@}. \]
<p>The constant multiple \( {@c@} \) just rides along; the old exponent \( {@n@} \) becomes the new coefficient factor and the power drops to \( {@m@} \).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
